<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Will and Testament — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Indian Succession Act 1925 (Sections 59 & 63), Registration Act 1908</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>No stamp paper mandatory (Can be written on clean paper, but e-Stamp ₹100 recommended)</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Optional under Section 18 Registration Act, but highly recommended at Sub-Registrar Office</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Mandatory attestation by minimum TWO independent witnesses who sign in testator's presence</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Probate Court / High Court / District Judge having jurisdiction</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>Operative only upon the demise of the Testator</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Doctor's Medical Fitness Certificate certifying sound mind of Testator; Title Deeds and Account details of all bequeathed properties; Aadhaar Cards and Passport Photos of Testator and Two Witnesses</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">WILL AND TESTAMENT</div>
<div class="draft-body">LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT

I, __________________________________________________, S/o __________________________________, aged _____ years, residing at ______________________________________________________________________, declare this to be my Last Will and Testament, revoking all former wills.

1. I am in sound health and disposing state of mind without any coercion or undue influence.
2. I appoint ________________________________________ as the sole Executor of this Will.
3. BEQUEST OF IMMOVABLE PROPERTY: My property bearing No. ____________ situated at ________________________ shall devolve absolutely upon my son/daughter/spouse, ________________________________________.
4. BEQUEST OF MOVABLE ASSETS: Bank accounts, Fixed Deposits, and shares shall devolve upon ________________________________________.

TESTATOR: _____________________________________

ATTESTATION BY WITNESSES:
We, the undersigned witnesses, declare that the Testator signed this Will in our joint presence, and we have signed as witnesses in the presence of the Testator and of each other.
Witness 1: ____________________________        Witness 2: ____________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>